Item 05 is complete. Everything required is in place: §5 written, the checks logged, PROGRESS.md and iterations.md updated, the gate passed on the final module. Seven items remain open, so no `LOOP_COMPLETE` line.

**What the item found.** The chain count `C_k(G)`, the number of layouts of vertex separation at most `k`, is exactly the number of solutions of a sparse bounded-degree polynomial system, but only in `Θ(n² k)` variables as counted and never fewer than `n(n − 1)`. It is also the solution count of a rank system in `n ⌈log₂ n⌉` variables with `n − 1` constraints of width `n ⌈log₂ n⌉`. The item's dichotomy is therefore a trade-off, and the incidence is `Θ(n²)` either way. The threshold's width is real as an equation (full degree and exponentially many monomials on most graphs) but compiles away at linear cost per cut, with communication rank `O(n)`. What does not compile away is that each cut test depends on every vertex (all set variables essential on every connected graph to 7 vertices at the refutation level) and there are `n − 1` tests on `n − 1` distinct sets. The exact count needs at least `log₂ n!` bits on `K_n`, above the verified budget from `n = 11`. The sieve over supports, the one identity on record that moves a permutation sum onto the `n`-cube, returns the lattice sum here.

**Verdict.** Plan §0.6's chain-count kill is met, with its parenthetical corrected: the structural obstacle is the ordering through its cuts, not the threshold's width. §5.7 states what item 09's one-session attempt would be if it is made, and PROGRESS.md suggests the coordinator may prefer to give that session to item 07.

**Checks.** Zero failures on every graph to 7 vertices: 8,475 chain counts three ways, 1,391 CaDiCaL model counts of the nested-chain CNF, 1,538 rank counts, 1,405 sieve identities, the two polynomial lemmas, `K_n` to 7. One refuter subagent found no wrong lemma but caught an odd-`n` bug in the split enumeration (fixed, check rerun, one "full rank" claim withdrawn), the `Θ(n²)` headline, and two over-stated sentences in §5.7, all folded in and listed in §5.9.

**Gate.** PASS twice, the second time on the final module: `lake build` clean, no `sorry`, no `axiom`, 1,958 tests passed, 123 solver tests passed, paper check clean. Nothing committed, `solutions/` untouched, no instance run, nothing downloaded, no Lean file changed.

